# backend.rules
version: 1

## MUST
- All SQL must use parameterized queries or a query builder/ORM; no string-concatenated SQL.
- All external input (request body, params, query, headers) is validated before use.
- No `any` in TypeScript; use proper types or `unknown` with narrowing.
- Every new endpoint has an explicit authentication/authorization check, or a one-line comment stating why it's intentionally public.

## SHOULD
- New endpoints are covered by at least one integration test.
- Error responses do not leak internal stack traces or implementation details to the client.

## SECURITY
- No secrets, API keys, or database credentials in code, in config committed to the repo, or in logs.
- No deprecated or known-vulnerable crypto primitives (e.g. MD5/SHA1 for passwords, ECB mode).
- Rate-limiting or equivalent abuse protection is considered for any new public endpoint.

## ARCHITECTURE
- Business logic lives in service/domain modules, not in route/controller handlers.
- Database access is isolated behind a repository/data-access layer, not scattered across services.
